A||||53||MinnGreenGT||Thoughts on a Fiero roof-scoop?||||5||
Z||000000||MinnGreenGT||12-19-2001||03:17 PM||||Ok... before anybody goes off screaming "ricer"- go watch a <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum6/HTML/004900.html" TARGET=_blank>rally race.</A>  That's where this type of design got started.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I'm curious as to people's thoughts about doing a roof scoop on a Fiero.  I'm thinking something along these lines:<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.wholesalehyperformance.com/digital-camera-pics1/roof-scoop1.jpg"> <BR><FONT SIZE="1">photo courtsey of <A HREF="http://www.wholesalehyperformance.com" TARGET=_blank>Wholesale Hyperformance</A> cost: $150</FONT><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ffeclipse1a.jpg"> <BR><FONT SIZE="1">This is the eclipse used in "The Fast & The Furious... just to see what it looks like on a finished piece.</FONT><P>I know it could be used to vent into the passenger compartment, although I'd prefer to find a way to get it to vent into the engine comparment (without blocking the entire rear window).<P>Just wondering what people's thoughts are on something like this...?  I'm currently starting work on some body mods- and will shortly require a new paint job (same/similiar color).  I'm really just "thinking out loud" on this one for now.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Joe Torma||12-19-2001||03:21 PM||||Damn, another secret project revealed.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>I've got something like that in mind.  Thats a nice looking scoop.  Not sure on how I'm going to do it yet...have a few ideas though.<P>------------------<BR>Its never going to be finished...<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig2_2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||RedHaze86SD4||12-19-2001||03:28 PM||||I've seen it on an mr2. the guy had it v out the back and 2 intakes going into the decklid area on either side of the back window. Basicaly just v it off the roof and go down into the air vents but dont close them all the way off. Maybe ad elec. fans to pull air out of the remaining area. Well that be best if you use the scoop for the intake.. <BR>just my thoughts anyways  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dumba$$||12-19-2001||03:42 PM||||i think that my sun roof would kind of be in the way  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Rich<BR>Sioux Falls SD<BR>Red 84 SE<BR>Gold 86 SE <BR>98 acura cl 3.0<P>ever notice that people that own a fiero, either have, or have had other fieros?||||reg||1
Z||000004||TRiAD||12-19-2001||04:43 PM||||I might delete the sunroof for that... <BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAAAMsSN*Wryq60N*CeWB!hXjfeIaMEc1YxPH9aPzaIXm!17ZpdBFE0Yk*d*dHNFG*GR3SFyLa8KJgh1IKe2Q/xmas-sig.jpg">       <BR><B><I><FONT COLOR="red">Merry Christmas!</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">Project MR1 ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</B><BR>Photoshop rendition of planned modifications<BR>AIM ~ Michael Blue 72</I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroBUZZ||12-19-2001||05:53 PM||||Just a thought, but it may be possible to remove all or part of the rear window and replace it with double panes of plexi or lexan (like a thermopane window). The space in between could be used to pass the air to the rear compartment.<BR>Gary||||reg||1
Z||000006||Philphine||12-19-2001||06:08 PM||||i thought about trying something like that for my chopper. also considered one of those pro-street scoops peeking over the roof like an indy scoop, but since i have an indy scoop on my other fiero and i like it i decided to get another. it's made for it and really dosen't block your view as much as you might think (my wing gives me more sight problems). ||||reg||1
Z||000007||reddog||12-19-2001||06:43 PM||||I like it, But while you develop that why not look into a dual scoop set-up that lets you keep your sunroof. (Lots of fieros with sunroofs out there!!!!) <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||tomanyfieros||12-19-2001||06:49 PM||||i have talked to my dad bout something like that, but he brought up the ?', where would the air go? i might just buy one of those and put on my 87 SE...<BR>Thanx Jason<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/dreamer.gif">    <BR><B>We all have dreams, but not everyone gets them...</B>||||reg||1
Z||000009||Sage||12-19-2001||09:04 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/srs_01.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/srs_02.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/srs03.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/srs_04.jpg"> <P>Here are some pics of one that my son started about a year ago.  It is similar to the one pictured above in an earlier post, but it incorporates a panel that replaces the sunroof, using the same mounting system.  It is not even in a medium "roughed in" stage here, but that is as far as he took it.  He had plans to do ducting that would channel the air down into the engine bay, introducing cool air in and letting the stock vents serve their original function with some "help" from above,LOL, OR he was just gonna put it on there to look "racy" and enjoy the wind in his hair without having a convertible.  <P>Not looking for opinions, just sharing one of his "went by the wayside" projects since it is along the same lines as this thread, and thought ya'll might enjoy knowing that somebody else was kicking the same idea around!<P><BR>Peace  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000010||BlackDragon||12-19-2001||09:17 PM||||i have thought about adding two smaller similar scoops. i figured that way you could still see out the back window a little. you could then duct it to the engine bay....... well, come to think of it, i would also put a camera on the deck, and an lcd screen where the rear veiw is  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> speakers filling the back glass  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <P>hey, i can dream!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||dcaprio||12-19-2001||09:19 PM||||I saw a fiero with the over the roof scoop that blended into a Indy scoop. I looked real good. I tried to find it on the web but I think the website I saw it on is gone.||||reg||1
Z||000012||Shaft||12-19-2001||09:28 PM||||I remember seeing some pics from Daytona this year that had a green fiero with a small roof scoop. I on't think it was ducted anywhere though. I think I have the pics on my comp somewhere.||||reg||1
