Z||000037||GodSend||12-20-2001||02:27 PM||||FieroMaster, how functional are the scoops that replaced your fastback windows?||||reg||1
Z||000038||The Fieromaster||12-20-2001||02:35 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by GodSend:<BR><B>FieroMaster, how functional are the scoops that replaced your fastback windows?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Honestly... Very.  You can actually see the lines in the paint from the dirt in the air scratching the paint over time (crappy paint job) and how they (the scoops) change the flow pattern of air...  Actually redirects the high speed air across the top of the vents drawing the hot air out at a faster rate than normally would and then off the back of the deck lid!  Its pretty cool!  I had my buddy toss pieces of paper out window at different points (he stayed in car as to not disrupt air flow) to see how the scoops moved the air!  Then i removed sunroof and he stood outta it on freeway and was feelin the air commin through the scoop and across the deck.  He said it was surprising how much they really caught!<p>[This message has been edited by The Fieromaster (edited 12-20-2001).]||||reg||1
