Z||000043||gggg-us||12-21-2001||06:38 PM||||Ok. how about dual scoops... You might be able to fabricate a set of scoops that fit in the exact place that the metal screens fit in on either side of the read deck...and funnel the air toward the center of the bay...this would work for air flor really well if scoop was on the deck lid.  Would make for some nice airflow, especially if you designed a special deck lid and scoops so that there was more vertical space between the screen and the frame...if that makes any sense.<P>Some pluses about this I guess...if it was made to fit where the screens are, then is would work on both coupes and GT's, and require no body modification, just pull out your old screens and insert new ones. If you were to make something like that, I'd be very interested in purchasing a pair...since I dont' know much about fabricating new body parts... You would want to make the new part with some rubber bumpers on it, so that it would basically rest on the top of the car, but not dammage the paint, and if you made the scoops short enough...the duals wouldn't interfere with a sunroof.<P>------------------<BR>88 4Cyl ... Rebuilding 81 Vette Engine for it now.||||reg||1
