Z||000048||Formula||12-22-2001||11:29 AM||||the neon has either a 2.0L SOHC or a 2.0L DOHC.  The reason why a lot of people turbo the chrysler motor is because it lasts longer then 70k miles turbo charged.  The mitsubishi motor suffers from crank walk.<P>Neons never came with a 1.8 L motor, always been a 2.0 SOHC (135 HP, 120 TQ..Base, expresso 4 dr, etc..)for economy and a 2.0 L DOHC for performance (150 hp, 140? TQ..R/T, sport, expresso 2 dr, etc..)<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dbelanger1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000049||Smoooooth GT||12-22-2001||12:47 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/F&F_MOTOR.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/F_&F_SUPRA.jpg"> <P>700 HP---- That's the "real" Supra also!!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooooothgtsig_9.gif">                       <BR>      <P><A HREF="http://www.thefibersmith.com" TARGET=_blank>www.thefibersmith.com</A>   <BR>Technical  Support (903) 825-7744 Steve<BR>"Smoooooth GT"<BR>Shaved door handles, sidetrim, exhaust outlet's, etc.... smooooth!!!||||reg||1
Z||000050||The Fieromaster||12-22-2001||10:14 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Formula:<BR><B>the neon has either a 2.0L SOHC or a 2.0L DOHC.  The reason why a lot of people turbo the chrysler motor is because it lasts longer then 70k miles turbo charged.  The mitsubishi motor suffers from crank walk.<P>Neons never came with a 1.8 L motor, always been a 2.0 SOHC (135 HP, 120 TQ..Base, expresso 4 dr, etc..)for economy and a 2.0 L DOHC for performance (150 hp, 140? TQ..R/T, sport, expresso 2 dr, etc..)<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Dbelanger1.jpg">  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>First off none repeat... None of the 1g's ever suffered from crank walk... crank walk is a problem that began in 96 after DSM desolved!  As for 70K thats bs too... IF your 2L is going to crank walk it will happen before you even hit the 30,000 mile mark!  Dont believe? Go to <A HREF="http://www.dsmtalk.com" TARGET=_blank>www.dsmtalk.com</A>  and ask ANYONE they will tell you the same thing.  The chrysler motor is J-unk! It has alot of torque compaired to the non turbo Mitsu 2L but its internals arent as strong!  Besides its easier to turbo a Mitsu 2L because it bolts right on!  Also turboing any 2g that wasnt turboed can be a pain cause its a OBDII system where as 1g's were OBDI...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> Id just rather stick with an engine that is ALREADY turboed... DSM 2L can handle 600hp stock according to Buscher racing.. <A HREF="http://www.buscherracing.com!" TARGET=_blank>www.buscherracing.com!</A> <P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">        <FONT COLOR="red"><B>"Raced That, Wrecked Better"</FONT></B>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif">   <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/thefieromastersig.gif">    <BR><B>~In Memory Of Jesse Cesek~ 1980-2000</B><BR><FONT COLOR="blue"><B>AOL IM: Fieromaster</B></FONT><BR><B><FONT COLOR="purple">1985 GT ~ Purple, Black and Yellow Interior(Fastback Converted)</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="maroon">1997 Mitsu Eclipse GSX ~ Maroon w/ Hella Balls!(GSX = AWD, Turbo) DOA on 12/10/2000</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="green">1992 Mitsubishi Eclipse GS ~ soon will be turboed</FONT><BR></B>||||reg||1
